# Rules placed in the private partition have access to core system types
# "map" is a separate permission from "read" since Android 10, and libc mmaps
# the per-context property area rather than read()ing it -- so read/open/getattr
# alone still leave a denial. Without map, DroidGuard (com.google.android.gms.
# unstable) stalls every IDroidGuardHandle call for 129s-390s, GMS then sends
# droidguard_results=null to android.clients.google.com/auth, and Play sign-in
# dies with "Add account completed with status=Unknown" ("Something went wrong").
# Verified 2026-09-18: adding map live via `ksud sepolicy patch` took the same
# binder call from 129021ms to 1453ms and stopped all 70 denials.
allow gmscore_app adbd_prop:file { read open getattr map };
allow gmscore_app adb_data_file:dir { getattr search };

